  "final_message": "I am checking the repository status and will review the codebase shortly.\nI am listing the files in the repository.\nI am checking recent commits.\nI am searching for all usages of `channel` across the codebase.\nI am searching for deprecation references across the codebase.\nI am running the test suite to establish a baseline.\nI am waiting for `npm test` to finish.\nI'll wait for the test suite to finish running.\nI am checking dependency-cruiser rules.\nI'll wait for the architecture check to complete.\nI'll wait for the task to finish.\nI am checking the git log diff.\nI am checking git log details.\nI cannot remove `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [`GEMINI.md`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Contract Integrity**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is a shared public contract consumed by downstream services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` constitutes a breaking subtractive change to deployed consumers.\n2. **Order Model Dependency**: The internal [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) entity supplies `channel` to [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) when publishing events and is part of the `POST /orders` contract in `createApp`.\n3. **Deprecation Path**: Per ARCH-4, fields cannot be abruptly deleted. Any phase-out must follow a formal deprecation lifecycle (e.g., marking `channel` with JSDoc `@deprecated`, coordinating deprecation timelines with consumer service teams, and incrementing event schema versions before physical removal).\n",
